n950-fm (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The FM sound: over the WL1273's I2S port (the sound card "N950 FM",
    kernel patches 0043-0045) instead of the TWL5031's AUX inputs, which
    carry silence. n950-fm-bt sends the Bluetooth vendor command that
    routes the chip's audio interface to FM (as FM apps under Harmattan
    do), n950-fm-audio then plays the card through a loopback.
  * Set the chip's volume after every power on: since radio-wl1273
    restores the last volume, the 1 left by switching off muted the radio.

 -- Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:45:00 +0100

n950-fm (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The Pro1X's FM radio (pro1x-maemo-leste apps/pro1x-fm, cd36dc6) for the
    N950's WL1273: the receiver switched on by VIDIOC_S_TUNER and off at
    the end, RDS decoded from raw blocks, the chip's RSSI as the signal,
    the sound through the TWL5031's AUX inputs (n950-fm-audio).

 -- Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0100
